  "summary": "A reusable phishing kit impersonates Calendly booking pages for fake Meta job interviews to steal Facebook and Google credentials, including 2FA codes and phone-prompt approvals relayed in real time. The kit polls an attacker collection server (AWS API Gateway in ap-southeast-1) to drive the victim's screen flow and carries version 0.8.0 plus a Vietnamese production-deployment comment. Victims are lured through 'join'-prefixed recruiting-themed domains on the .cfd, .info and .works TLDs.",
